! dogfood-stand-runbook.md — plan, 2026-11-08

Verbatim scratch record `.lares-scratch/controller/dogfood-stand-runbook.md` (plan, file date 2026-11-08); only Markdown transliterated to memetic-wikitext, its words kept as written. Index: [[workshop index|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/workshop/controller/index]].

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/dogfood-stand-runbook`>>

! Dogfood stand — runbook (operator ruling 2026-11-07: "Pono, approve the dogfood/keeper split.")

A DOGFOOD hearth: re-standable as often as needed (single-operator re-found, 2026-10-31). The keeper rite keeps every qualification. Source: founding-runbook #/prepare, #/pre-rite, #/found; the landmark map's M4 route. The seat prepares 1-3; the operator's hands run 4 on an attached TTY.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/0-ready-state`>>

!! 0. Ready state (operator, 2026-11-07, item 4)
The main repo reaches the full ready-to-dogfood state (every gate lane landed, the span green), then a FULL rebuild (`pnpm build` and the product image at the landed head), then the check that the live Lararium launches containerized, web3 and local-first.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/1-gate`>>

!! 1. Gate (seat)
* Lanes: lease-end slice 2, L23 and the harness batch land; P27 PARKED (CI reds real boots; the old deciders stand).
* The dogfood proof set (lane `dogfood-proof`, a deterministic e2e set reusing existing suites first) reads green in CI: the stand, memory surviving a re-stand (L9 re-pour reproduces), the MCP seat's meme_put/meme_get round-trip, a booted vessel mounting its islands with no manifest refusal, the containerized web3 local-first launch.
* The span's CI and held-out read green at the head the image builds from.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/2-homes`>>

!! 2. Homes (seat prepares, nothing deleted)
* State home, kept across re-stands: `~/.lares/state`, named by `~/.lares/lares-surface.env` (the env the `lares` MCP seat already reads, so the seat reaches the hearth unchanged). The old walk's state there renames aside first: `mv ~/.lares/state ~/.lares/state.before-dogfood && mkdir ~/.lares/state`.
* Workspace: THE MAIN REPO (operator, 2026-11-07: the workspace question mu'd). `LARES_WORKSPACE=/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine`. Live wiki and canon writes land in the tracked tree as source-control write-back. Branch plan (operator, 2026-11-07): once the dogfood stands AND the proof set reads green, all outstanding work merges into `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5`, that merges to `main`, and the primary repo checks out ONE root branch, `develop`, where the house both dogfoods and develops until the roadmap clears; milestones PR back to `main`. No split: lanes branch off `develop` and land into it; the live wiki's writes land on `develop` too.
* A re-stand renames the old state home aside (`mv ~/.lares-hearth ~/.lares-hearth.<label>`), never deletes; memories re-pour by content key (L9) from the old projection.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/3-image`>>

!! 3. Image (seat, LAST, at the landed head)
`cd $LARES_WORKSPACE && GIT_REV=$(git rev-parse HEAD) docker compose -f docker-compose.surface.yml build lares` and read `org.opencontainers.image.revision` back.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/4-the-stand`>>

!! 4. The stand (operator's hands, attached TTY, in $LARES_WORKSPACE with both vars exported)
```sh
tools/lares-container.sh found --hearth --name '<label>' --chair '<chair>'   # route + cold-key card read-back on paper
tools/lares-container.sh up                                                    # live unlock on the TTY
tools/lares-container.sh vessel seed --apply --yes
tools/lares-container.sh vessel read
tools/lares-container.sh persona list --json
tools/lares-container.sh nexus seal show
tools/lares-container.sh meme list --recipe default --json
```
(`found --hearth` founds persona zero whole; the runbook's separate `persona new 0` line is drift the canon pass trues.)

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/5-read-backs`>>

!! 5. Read-backs (seat, after the stand)
* `<state>/wikis/kahua-<tag>` and `<state>/bags/kahua-<tag>` exist; no `bags/daemon` anywhere (the rite stops there otherwise).
* The `lares` MCP seat connects to the standing daemon; `meme_put` then `meme_get` round-trips one tiddler; the file lands in the projection.
* Then the M5 spine opens: L17 MCP full TW5 caps, L8/L10/L11, L18, L19 (the flat memories move in), L13.

<<~/ahu>>

